## Cross-cutting policy (reading-3)

- **Standalone text + captions; code only in annexes** (canonical
  re-articulation of finding 22, see [[0606]]): main text and captions
  are standalone at the maths/ideas level with `\ref` to annexes; only
  annexes reference the code implementation. Goes in docs/editorial-brief.md.
- **§3 restructure** ([[0602]]): split the Evaluation material into a
  standalone Scoring Annex A (hierarchical scoring + four dimensions in
  turn + owns figure S1, shortened caption), referenced from §3 as the
  implementation. Reorders the appendix — watch annex-letter refs.

## Wave plan (mirrors 0578)

1. Author declares reading-3 finished.
2. Organize children into a raid order (sequence the main.tex-contact
   tickets to avoid same-file conflicts; intro tickets 0602/0603/0604 all
   touch the intro region — stack or sequence them; 0598 spans intro +
   §7.2 + Conclusion + annex; 0601 is caption-only; 0600 is §exp2; 0602
   adds an annex + code-aligned maths).
3. Execute in worktree-isolated waves; each child PR gated (review +
   verify-gate) before merge.
4. Red-team verify ALL findings against post-merge main (refute-by-default,
   the 0578 method).
5. Close this tracker after the integration review passes.

